<p class="foot">This is a browser reconstruction of the historical <b>b=a</b> limiting setup. Its selected contact obeys the analytic no-slip condition at one nominated point; because equal radii create a nonisolated contact set, this does <b>not</b> certify no-slip across every point of contact. There is no separate pen or projector. The only tracing member is the gimbal elbow, constrained perpendicular to the moving crossbar. GrAnn is represented by a **selected-contact great-circle carrier** that constrains P_ivot to the outer torus wall and its antipode to Donomphulon on the inner wall; the outer/inner diameter is BigRad. The historical GrAnn_Omph self-intersection at i_r and GrAnn_t_ipode self-tangency are NOT yet reconstructed. Two independently shaped source curves share a sweep clock; signed curvature differences change elbow orientation. This is not a certified physical bearing model. No isomorphism or physical law is assumed. Research reference: <a href="https://github.com/Satobloc/HsH/tree/main/tools/whirligig_rq">Whirligig R/Q Python solver</a>.</p></main>
