[L2]   "content": "# Podcast Guide — current authority note

**Status:** CURRENT PUBLIC PRESENTATION ROUTER / source crosswalk pending  
**Established:** 2026-09-20 by Nathan directive

Current strongest known public episode-guide surface:

`https://glass-sausage-factory.nathanmcknight.chatgpt.site/podcast`

Treat this page as the **default current public guide to the podcast corpus** unless a newer Nathan directive or a more complete source-backed index supersedes it.

## Authority boundary

This means:
- use it first for public episode discovery, organization, navigation, and site-facing podcast references;
- prefer its current structure over older partial episode guides when choosing a public-facing route;
- crosswalk important episode/date/title/description claims back to primary podcast/feed/archive metadata when provenance matters;
- do not treat page placement, summaries, or curation as theory authority;
- do not infer that every underlying episode record has already been independently source-audited merely because the guide is currently the most useful/complete presentation surface.

## Maintenance goal

Build toward a durable repository-side podcast index that can reproduce or feed the public guide while preserving:
- canonical episode title;
- publication/date metadata;
- duration where available;
- audio/source URL;
- description/show notes;
- topic/concept tags;
- relevant SAT/H(s)H historical phase;
- source/provenance status;
- transcript/conversation links where available;
- public-guide URL/slug.

Until that crosswalk is mature, the live podcast page is the preferred presentation router and the archive/feed/source record remains the preferred provenance authority.

## Access note

The current orchestration environment could not directly retrieve the `chatgpt.site` page through its web-fetch backend on 2026-09-20. This is an access limitation, not evidence against the page or its contents. Workers with direct page access should use it and report material structure/index changes into the public-site continuity layer.
