<div class="head"><div><h3>Whirligig · conjugate two-crossbar prototype</h3><div class="sub">One rolling sphere · two independent follower bars · counter-rotating gimbals · one rim-anchored meridional pointer</div></div><div class="sub mono" id="state">ψ = 0.000 rad</div></div>
<div class="controls">
  <button id="play">Pause</button><button id="reset">Reset</button>
  <label>Orbit <input id="scrub" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.001" value="0"><span id="scrubv">0%</span></label>
  <label>Speed <input id="speed" type="range" min="0.15" max="2.5" step="0.05" value="0.75"><span id="speedv">0.75×</span></label>
  <label><input id="showtrace" type="checkbox" checked> primary trace</label>
  <label><input id="showslice" type="checkbox" checked> bagelwise slice</label>
</div>
<div class="layout">
  <div class="panel"><canvas id="scene" width="1000" height="645"></canvas><div class="legend">
    <span class="key"><i class="sw" style="background:#edc879"></i> A crossbar</span>
    <span class="key"><i class="sw" style="background:#e18fca"></i> B crossbar</span>
    <span class="key"><i class="sw" style="background:#77d2e8"></i> A elbow / Curvy Lisa</span>
    <span class="key"><i class="sw" style="background:#f0b86c"></i> B rim pointer</span>
    <span class="key"><i class="sw" style="background:#a6b4fa"></i> selected sphere contact</span>
  </div></div>
  <div class="side">
    <div class="panel"><canvas id="body" width="480" height="380"></canvas><div class="status">Sphere-body view: R and Q remain separate input curves; the Analemma is shown in violet. Demo inputs: R = cos(2λ) + 3/11 sin(3λ); Q = sin(3λ) + 1/6 cos(5λ).</div></div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><b>Phase lock</b><span id="phaseMetric">A +4 · B −4</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Rim pointer</b><span id="pointerMetric">3 turns / orbit</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Wobble differential</b><span id="wobbleMetric">—</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Mirror residual</b><span id="mirrorMetric">—</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Primary wall hits</b><span id="hitMetric">—</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Trace seam</b><span id="seamMetric">—</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Largest step</b><span id="jumpMetric">—</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>Current torus coords</b><span id="coordMetric">—</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel"><div class="sub">Current follower parameters</div><div class="mono" id="followerMetric" style="margin-top:5px;color:#e8eee9">—</div><div class="sub" style="margin-top:8px">Torus scale</div><div class="mono" style="color:#e8eee9">b = a = 0.550 · R = 2.873033 · R/b = 5.223697</div></div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="foot"><span class="warn">Prototype interpretation:</span> the B elbow's horizontal azimuth sets the azimuth of its independent pointer anchor on the inner rim. The pointer is radial through the torus center and outer circumference, so its meridional plane slices the torus. The B elbow itself remains a separate counter-rotating gimbal. No A/B linkage is introduced. Drag the main view to rotate the camera.</div>
</div>
